  "title": "GPT Image grows beyond generation",
  "summary": "May brought more control over images and text, easier ways to build with Pollinations, and a growing directory of community projects.\n\nThe image API added `gptimage`, then gained editing, quality settings, and edits using multiple image URLs. Prompt translation and image error handling also received fixes.\n\nText requests gained a larger character limit, new model options, JSON Schema forwarding, and sampling controls. Model listings became more precise, while streaming responses and cache reuse got steadier.\n\nThe MCP server gained a local `npx` setup path and later OAuth 2.1 for clients. WebSim added prompt-generated, single-file HTML with a selectable model; guides clarified MCP setup and audio responses.\n\nCommunity additions ranged from chat and writing tools to image apps, coding interfaces, accessibility software, and bots. The directory also gained a Vibe Coding category and cleaner featured-project ordering.",
